Okay, so you already know that you can get teleportitis from something
you eat.  It's a pretty big hint if you watch the behavior of the
creatures, but that's only obvious after the fact, huh?  So when you 
ate the corpse, you got a message ("You feel jumpy!").

What you want, though, is teleport control first.  There's a ring that 
does that.  Unfortunately, identifying rings is a challenge.  If I have
a ring that I think might be Teleport Control, and I'm ready to risk it, 
I try it on next to a teleport trap, and jump on the trap.  Take it off 
immediately if it's not...

One of the most sought-after events in the early part of the game is the
Tengu.  Tengu are frustrating because they might either give you
teleportitis or teleport control, but you don't know which you'll get.
So unfortunately it's a risk.  It helps to have a tinning kit.  If
you're one of those players who gets really lucky, there are ways to 
eat rings.  That carries more uncertainty than my tastes allow, so it
never happens.  Maybe if I accidentally found myself as a metallivore
and sitting on a pile of extra rings, then it would make sense.



